{"resourceIdentifier":"3649","resourceName":"Tianjin Dahanzhuang LFG Power Generation Project I","description":"Tianjin Dahanzhuang LFG Power Generation ProjectⅠ(hereinafter referred to as the Project) is located at the Dahanzhuang landfill site in Balitai town, Jinnan District, Tianjin city, P.R China.The purpose of the project is to capture and utilize landfill gas for power generation. The electricity generated by the project is supplied to North China Power Grid (NCPG). The new gas extraction and utilization systems have been installed by the project. Before the implementation of the project activity, the landfill gas that was captured and utilized by the project was emitted into the atmosphere directly. Equivalent electricity was provided by North China Power Grid (NCPG) which is dominated by coal-fired power stations. This is the scenario that existed prior to the implementation of the project activity and is also the baseline scenario.\r\nIn absence of the project, the equivalent amount of electricity exported to the grid by the project would have otherwise been supplied by North China Power Grid (NCPG). Greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions will be reduced by avoiding CO2 emissions from those fossil fuel-based power plants connected to the grid and by avoiding GHG emissions from releasing LFG into the atmosphere from the landfill site.","location":{"latitude":38.951861,"longitude":117.284975},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-09-21","endExclusive":"2022-10-22","endInclusive":"2022-10-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3649"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Tianjin"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Tianjin Zhonglan Huanneng Co., Ltd"},{"type":"string","value":"Tianjin, China"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type"